# CEO communication (Pocock-adapted)

**Audience:** Founder / CEO — builds with AI, **not** a full-time developer.

**Canon:** Matt Pocock — *sacrifice grammar for concision.* Fragments OK. Plain words only.

## Rules

1. **Outcome first** — what happened / what you need → then why (one line).
2. **Sacrifice grammar** — drop filler (`just`, `basically`, `I think`); short sentences or fragments OK.
3. **Plain English** — gloss jargon once in 2–6 words; reuse short term after.
4. **No dev assumed** — no file paths, TypeScript, or "review the diff" unless CEO says "go deep".
5. **Scannable** — bullets; bold only for **action** or **blocker**.
6. **Depth opt-in** — CEO says "go deep" / "show technical" → then details.
7. **In-app / tour copy** — same bar (see `guided-tours.mdc`).

## Pattern

```text
**Bottom line:** <one sentence outcome>

**What happened**
- <fact>

**You** (only if human action)
- <one step> — or "Nothing — agent handles it"
```

## PP glossary (CEO-facing)

| Term | Say |
|------|-----|
| Ralph | Auto chain — merge → next agent task |
| Slice | One packaged task (e.g. FM-3) |
| Merge | Change live in main repo |
| AFK | Agent runs without you in chat |
| Notify only | Chain paused — report only, no new task |

Incident tone examples: [`.cursor/skills/session-report/references/ralph-incidents.md`](../skills/session-report/references/ralph-incidents.md)

## MUST NOT

- Walls of prose
- Ask CEO to read GitHub / diffs on AFK slices
- Alphabet soup without gloss unless CEO asked technical
